From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 21:50:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] strip: gut reliability.rs of cloud uploads + drop
 MINIDUMP_ENDPOINT

reliability.rs is now hang-tracing only: traces are written to disk
under paths::hang_traces_dir() but never uploaded. All reqwest/Sentry
multipart code, upload_previous_minidumps, upload_minidump, and
upload_build_timings are gone, along with the diagnostics-enabled gate
and feature-flags coupling.

Also removes:
 - client::telemetry::MINIDUMP_ENDPOINT (env: ZED_MINIDUMP_ENDPOINT).
 - The cx.subscribe(&user_store, ...) block in main.rs that forwarded
   the metrics_id / is_staff bits into crashes::set_user_info.

The crashes crate itself is retained: it still captures local minidumps
(remote_server depends on it and the local minidump files are useful
for the user themselves), it just no longer phones home.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
